the fraction, multiply every term by 3:\n\\[\n3y - 3 \\log_2 3 = y.\n\\]\n\nRearrange to isolate \\(y\\):\n\\[\n3y - y = 3 \\log_2 3 \\implies 2y = 3 \\log_2 3 \\implies y = \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(y = \\log_2 (\\log_2 x)\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\log_2 (\\log_2 x) = \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nLet \\(z = \\log_2 x\\). Then the equation becomes:\n\\[\n\\log_2 z = \\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nBy exponentiating both sides with base 2, we get:\n\\[\nz = 2^{\\frac{3 \\log_2 3}{2}} = (2^{\\log_2 3})^{\\frac{3}{2}} = 3^{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\sqrt{27}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(z = \\log_2 x\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\log_2 x = \\sqrt{27}.\n\\]\n\nWe are asked to find \\((\\log_2 x)^2\\):\n\\[\n(\\log_2 x)^2 = (\\sqrt{27})^2 = 27.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
